# Local (build-host/selinux-fixes.sh): label memfds with their creator's domain in the memfd_file class.
# Android 17's platform policy is written for it (binder_call, appdomain and isolated_app memfd_file rules),
# but nothing enables the capability for vendor API 202504 devices. The 6.18 kernel supports it, and
# without it every memfd (sys.use_memfd: there is no /dev/ashmem) lands in tmpfs and is denied across binder.
policycap memfd_class;
